Third-party data
The maps are built from open data published by others: the Cities of Toronto,
Chicago and Vancouver, Statistics Canada, the U.S. Census Bureau, transit
agencies, OpenStreetMap, Wikipedia and others. That data stays under its
original licences, which are listed at https://layers.city/attributions/ and in
each city's SOURCES.md. Nothing here restricts what those licences allow. In
particular, data derived from OpenStreetMap remains available under the Open
Database License (ODbL), and text derived from Wikipedia under CC BY-SA.

Third-party software
Open-source libraries and fonts used by the site (for example Leaflet,
leaflet-polylineoffset, html-to-image, mapshaper, Archivo and IBM Plex) remain
under their own licences.

